From 6886f1e4c72e91bb611e24423684d3bd30f393b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:17:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Feat] [AMD] mooncake: Add the AMD_GEM custom memory pool for
 KV caches on ROCm

On amdgpu-dkms 6.18.4 through at least 7.1.9, and kernels without
torvalds/linux 9131cc85d0de (v7.4-rc1), the KFD allocation limit counts
device memory that a NIC pins twice. Once Mooncake registers a KV cache
larger than the VRAM left after allocating it, every later device
allocation of the process fails; the scheduler segfaults in
c10::hip::HIPStream::stream() at the first read of a new stream after the
registration.

SGLANG_MOONCAKE_CUSTOM_MEM_POOL=AMD_GEM allocates the KV pools with
mooncake.allocator.HipGemAllocator: amdgpu GEM BOs imported into HIP,
which the limit counts once. Unlike NVLINK and BAREX it only changes where
the pools live, so the KV transfer keeps the default batched path.
